fields.description:
Word select size. Sets the number of sclk cycles for which ws_out stays in the left and in the right cycle.

Usage: Write only while clken is 0. Choose a size not smaller than the audio word length of every enabled channel, otherwise the least significant bits are truncated.

Values:
0x0 16 sclk cycles (reset value of the default configuration);
0x1 24 sclk cycles;
0x2 32 sclk cycles;
0x3 64 sclk cycles;
0x4 128 sclk cycles;
0x5 256 sclk cycles.

Unit: sclk cycles.

Limits: 0x6 and 0x7 are reserved; sizes above 32 need the extended word-select configuration.

Serial clock gating. Selects after how many sclk cycles of a left or right cycle sclk_gate turns the clock off for the rest of that cycle.

Usage: Write only while clken is 0. The gating point must not exceed the largest programmed audio word length or data is truncated.

Values:
0x0 no gating (reset value of the default configuration);
0x1 gate after 12 sclk cycles;
0x2 gate after 16 sclk cycles;
0x3 gate after 20 sclk cycles;
0x4 gate after 24 sclk cycles;
0x5 gate after 32 sclk cycles.

Unit: sclk cycles.

Limits: 0x6 and 0x7 are reserved.

Receive word length. Number of valid audio bits per left or right word that the receiver stores, LSB aligned in the data register.

Usage: Write only while the channel (or, in TDM mode, the receiver block) is disabled. A value larger than the configured maximum resolution restores the configured maximum.

Values:
0x0 ignore the word length, use the configured maximum;
0x1 12 bits;
0x2 16 bits (reset value of the default configuration);
0x3 20 bits;
0x4 24 bits;
0x5 32 bits.

Unit: bits.

Limits: 0x6 and 0x7 are reserved; not larger than PARA_I2S_RX_WORDSIZE_0 to 3 of the channel.

Transmit word length. Number of valid audio bits per left or right word that the transmitter shifts out, MSB first.

Usage: Write only while the channel (or, in TDM mode, the transmitter block) is disabled. A value larger than the configured maximum resolution restores the configured maximum.

Values:
0x0 ignore the word length, use the configured maximum;
0x1 12 bits;
0x2 16 bits (reset value of the default configuration);
0x3 20 bits;
0x4 24 bits;
0x5 32 bits.

Unit: bits.

Limits: 0x6 and 0x7 are reserved; not larger than PARA_I2S_TX_WORDSIZE_0 to 3 of the channel.

FIFO depth encoding for small depths. Reports the FIFO depth of all channels when it is 16 entries or less.

Usage: Read by the driver to size DMA bursts and trigger levels.

Values:
0x0 2 entries;
0x1 4 entries;
0x2 8 entries (reset value);
0x3 16 entries.

Unit: entries.

Limits: valid only when the depth is 16 or less.
